From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:07:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally give the J604 eleven DVFS
 rows

The J604's own ADT lists sixteen GPU performance states, and they form
eleven distinct voltage rows: states 0 to 4 on their own (state 4 is
928 MHz at 725 mV), the equal-voltage pairs 5/6 to 13/14, and the top
state 15. The firmware takes ten or eleven rows. The J604 got the
J713's ten, so its layout leaves state 4 out, while macOS 26B123 runs
the J604 with eleven rows (its POWER_PERFORMANCE at INIT has a top of
1000).

Add g16_j604_rows11 (load time, default 0). When set on a J604, the
board takes eleven rows with the existing eleven-row map, whose
pairing check holds on the J604's values, so state 4 is kept and the
top state becomes S10. The host governor's top, the idle and board
floors, the cooling ceiling and the selector at the top follow the
table instead of a fixed S9, and with g16_fw_controllers=1 the
controller words that depend on the top take macOS's eleven-row
values. With the switch off nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
